  <data name="ScamCheckButtonText" xml:space="preserve"><value>Is this a scam?</value></data>
  <data name="ScamCheckTooltip" xml:space="preserve"><value>Check whether this page looks like a scam (worked out on your computer, no internet needed)</value></data>
  <data name="ScamLevelGreen" xml:space="preserve"><value>Green: no big warning signs found</value></data>
  <data name="ScamLevelYellow" xml:space="preserve"><value>Yellow: be careful, some warning signs</value></data>
  <data name="ScamLevelRed" xml:space="preserve"><value>Red: high risk, do not give money or details here</value></data>
  <data name="ScamEstimateNote" xml:space="preserve"><value>This is only an estimate, not a guarantee. Green does not mean there is no risk. If in doubt, give nothing and close the page.</value></data>
  <data name="ScamReasonsTitle" xml:space="preserve"><value>Why</value></data>
  <data name="ScamReasonNone" xml:space="preserve"><value>No suspicious signs were found.</value></data>
  <data name="ScamReasonOfficialSiteFormat" xml:space="preserve"><value>This is the real address of {0}.</value></data>
  <data name="ScamReasonKnownScamSite" xml:space="preserve"><value>This site is on the list of known scam sites.</value></data>
  <data name="ScamReasonSafeBrowsingFlag" xml:space="preserve"><value>Google Safe Browsing has marked this address as dangerous.</value></data>
  <data name="ScamReasonLookalikeFormat" xml:space="preserve"><value>The address looks like a copy of the real {0} address ({1}).</value></data>
  <data name="ScamReasonImpersonatesBrandFormat" xml:space="preserve"><value>The page uses the name {0} and asks for a password, PIN or OTP, but it is not the real {0} site.</value></data>
  <data name="ScamReasonBrandOnWrongDomainFormat" xml:space="preserve"><value>The page mentions {0}, but it is not the real {0} site.</value></data>
  <data name="ScamReasonPinOrOtpRequest" xml:space="preserve"><value>It asks for a PIN or OTP. Never give these to anyone except the real service.</value></data>
  <data name="ScamReasonCardDetailsRequest" xml:space="preserve"><value>It asks for card details.</value></data>
  <data name="ScamReasonFormSendsElsewhere" xml:space="preserve"><value>What you type would be sent to a different site.</value></data>
  <data name="ScamReasonUrgencyWords" xml:space="preserve"><value>It tries to rush you, for example by saying your account will be closed if you do not act now.</value></data>
  <data name="ScamReasonPrizeClaim" xml:space="preserve"><value>It says you won a prize or lottery, which is very common in scams.</value></data>
  <data name="ScamReasonSimOrKycThreat" xml:space="preserve"><value>It threatens SIM blocking or asks for KYC or NID verification.</value></data>
  <data name="ScamReasonJobOrMoneyOffer" xml:space="preserve"><value>It offers easy income from home, an advance fee or doubled money.</value></data>
  <data name="ScamReasonCountdownTimer" xml:space="preserve"><value>There is a countdown timer to pressure you.</value></data>
  <data name="ScamReasonSuspiciousAddress" xml:space="preserve"><value>The site address looks unusual (for example an odd ending, an IP number or many parts).</value></data>
  <data name="ScamReasonNoHttps" xml:space="preserve"><value>The connection is not secure (HTTPS), yet it asks for private details.</value></data>
  <data name="ScamAiTitle" xml:space="preserve"><value>Explanation from the AI on your computer (also an estimate)</value></data>
